  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 accuracy. The key uncertainty is whether the image modality's contribution is limited by the relatively weak ResNet50 encoder (image-only ResNet50 scored only 0.208). Config_039 changes only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other proven elements (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) identical to config_033. This isolates the effect of image encoder quality. If ViT-L's stronger pretrained visual features improve the multimodal result, it validates investing in a better image backbone; if not, it confirms the image modality's ceiling and we can focus remaining budget on RNA-side or fusion refinements. With 2 experiments left after this, a single-variable test on the most impactful untested dimension is the highest-value use of the next slot."
}

